            <ArticleTitle>Lumbar spinal cord stimulation for cervical-originated central pain: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>299-301</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case presents a patient with neuropathic pain in a lower extremity, which appeared subsequent to the removal of a C1 meningioma and which was successfully treated by lower thoracic spinal cord stimulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
